<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Even&nbsp;more&nbsp;stuff!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Man, the second one is way better than what I had in mind, and makes more sense with the findings in the additional entries. I think I'm gonna call that canon.</p>
<p>My initial idea was that the Society are scientists from &quot;somewhere else&quot; who may or may not be human and don't have the same kind of filters we do on what constitutes reasonable, ethical, or really even worthwhile research. When we made the immunity deal for Unit 731's data (and Operation Paperclip), they somehow got the impression that the US not only condoned that kind of research, but was in the market for more. The yellow journals/documentation are just how their communication comes out on our end.</p>
</div>
