			<div class="content" id="post-content-2127404">
									

<p>Thanks :) Actually no, although the Laundry Files is one of my favorite series.</p>
<p>All the library details are lifted from my old job, and the main inspiration was the thousands of actual yellow-bound conference proceedings we had to deal with. They were a pain in the ass to shelve/move, new ones came in all the time, literally nobody ever read them (because we had digital versions of all of them), but we weren't allowed to get rid of them.</p>
<p>The historical context came later.</p>
<p>Complete tangent: Although I loved the Atrocity Archives and I think Stross pulled it off rather well, I have mixed feelings about anything that tries to attribute a direct mystical or paranormal motivation for atrocities committed in WWII. I like to think that this one is more about unintended consequences than blood magic.</p>

