<p>Hah! A fellow Laundry fan. Did you read Rhesus Chart yet, perchance? (I'm kinda at a loss for people to talk about that one yet XD)</p>
<p>TBH, I don't mind what he does in AA - for one, it's one of the rare cases where it actually fits well and doesn't paint the fascists in a better light - I mean, it'd have been tasteless if it was them doing it to save the world or something, but [PLOT REDACTED] doesn't really do that.</p>
<p>Also, it's not really an unique thing among his work - have a look at Fuller Memorandum and the reinterpretation of baron Roman von Ungern-Sternberg, who, put succintly, wasn't a nice guy in the least. In both cases, he manages to fit in with the real material really really well.</p>
<p>On an unrelated note +1 for this article.</p>

